{#
/**
 * @file
 * Theme override to display a region.
 *
 * Available variables:
 * - content: The content for this region, typically blocks.
 * - attributes: HTML attributes for the region <div>.
 * - region: The name of the region variable as defined in the theme's
 *   .info.yml file.
 *
 * @see template_preprocess_region()
 */
#}
{#
  Everything in the footer is meta – the status line, the copyright and the
  sign-off – so the whole region keeps Geist Mono (agreed 2026-07-30). The
  status line arrives as a block body, which preprocess gives `prose`, and
  `prose` sets font-family on itself; `[&_p]:font-mono` targets the paragraph
  directly and lands in the utilities layer, which beats both that and the base
  layer's rule on `p`.

  `[&_.prose]:text-base` undoes the reading size for the same reason. The status
  line is a block body, and ncktrnr_tw_preprocess_field() gives every block body
  `prose` – which since 2026-07-30 ramps to 22px at lg, sizing a one-line footer
  note like an About paragraph. `not-prose` is no use here: it suppresses prose
  styling on descendants *of* a prose block, and this element is the prose block.
  The descendant selector carries two classes, so it beats `.prose` outright
  rather than depending on source order.

  This comment sits outside the `set` tag deliberately. Twig lexes the whole tag
  as one expression, so a comment opened inside the array is a syntax error and
  returns a 500 for every page carrying the region.
#}
{%
  set classes = [
    'region',
    'region-' ~ region|clean_class,
    'mx-auto',
    'container',
    'px-4',
    'pt-12',
    'pb-24',
    'flex',
    'flex-wrap',
    'justify-between',
    'gap-6',
    '[&_p]:font-mono',
    '[&_.prose]:text-base',
  ]
%}

{% if content %}
  <div{{ attributes.addClass(classes) }}>
    {{ content }}
    <div class="flex gap-x-8 font-mono">
      <div>©{{ 'now' | date('Y') }} ncktrnr</div>
      <div>Made with plants, 100% vegan</div>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endif %}
